cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Spectral-front identities for periodic Navier-Stokes and a
  conditional obstruction to uniform pointwise Osgood closure
message: >-
  If you refer to this work, please cite the archived release.
  This repository does not claim a solution to the Clay
  Navier-Stokes problem in either direction.
type: software
authors:
  # Replace this entry with the author's full name before minting a DOI.
  - name: HeliCorgi
    website: "https://github.com/HeliCorgi"
repository-code: "https://github.com/HeliCorgi/ns-singularity-certificate-lab"
abstract: >-
  For strong solutions of the unforced incompressible Navier-Stokes
  equations on the three-dimensional torus, the spectral bandwidth
  obeys an exact modal identity giving the monotone quantity
  Lambda = log N_0^2 - (1/2 nu) int K D, hence a bandwidth-dissipation
  dichotomy: finiteness of the action int K D forces the solution to be
  global. The action has the exact representation int K D =
  int |du/dt|^2/D + nu^2 int H_2/H_1 + nu log(D/D_0) and is dominated
  pointwise by both the Serrin (infinity,2) and the critical
  |grad u|_{L^3}^2 actions. Conditionally on one open, finitely
  certified lattice-sum hypothesis, an explicit coherent
  critical-spectrum family shows that no Osgood-admissible pointwise
  majorant K <= Phi(log N_0^2) can hold uniformly, so the dichotomy
  cannot be upgraded to unconditional regularity by that route.
  The repository also records, with exact-arithmetic certificates, the
  candidate mechanisms that were tested and rejected.
keywords:
  - Navier-Stokes
  - regularity criteria
  - spectral bandwidth
  - Osgood condition
  - computer-assisted mathematics
  - exact rational arithmetic
  - Lean 4
license: Apache-2.0
